## Phaser-Specific Notes

1. Use Phaser's scene lifecycle methods effectively:
   ```typescript
   // Initialize with data from previous scene
   init(data: any): void {
     // Set up scene with received data
   }
   
   // Preload scene-specific assets
   preload(): void {
     // Load assets needed for this scene only
   }
   
   // Set up the scene
   create(): void {
     // Create game objects, set up physics, etc.
   }
   
   // Game loop
   update(time: number, delta: number): void {
     // Frame-by-frame updates
   }
   ```

2. Handle scene transitions with data properly:
   ```typescript
   // Start a new scene and shut down this one
   this.scene.start('NextScene', { level: 2, score: currentScore });
   
   // Start a scene in parallel (overlay)
   this.scene.launch('PauseMenu', { returnScene: this.scene.key });
   
   // Put this scene to sleep (pause, but keep in memory)
   this.scene.sleep();
   
   // Resume a sleeping scene
   this.scene.wake();
   ```

3. Proper scene shutdown for resource management:
   ```typescript
   // Set up clean shutdown
   this.events.once('shutdown', () => {
     // Cancel timers
     this.time.removeAllEvents();
     
     // Remove event listeners
     this.input.keyboard.off('keydown-SPACE');
     this.events.off('resume');
     
     // Destroy game objects that won't be garbage collected
     this.tweens.killAll();
     
     // Stop any ongoing physics
     this.physics.world.shutdown();
   });
   ```

4. Use Phaser's built-in registry for simple cross-scene data:
   ```typescript
   // In any scene, set data
   this.registry.set('playerScore', 1000);
   
   // In any other scene, get the data
   const score = this.registry.get('playerScore');
   
   // Listen for registry changes
   this.registry.events.on('changedata', (parent, key, value) => {
     if (key === 'playerScore') {
       this.updateScoreDisplay(value);
     }
   });
   